# A restart after a notified WARNING: the REMOVED row the load injects copies the old row's flags, so it is the
# alarm's last executed event, and the alarm's first status is notified again: the WARNING it still has, and, in
# the next life, the CLEAR of an alert that was already clear.
database real
rules tests/corpus/notify/plain.conf
chart loop.n loop.n_name loop.notify disks things 1
label loop.n kind ssd
var loop.n v 10
clock 0
pass 0
var loop.n v 70
clock 1
pass 1
clock 2
pass 2
clock 100
restart
clock 101
pass 101
clock 102
pass 102
var loop.n v 10
clock 103
pass 103
clock 200
restart
clock 201
pass 201
clock 202
pass 202
clock 203
alarm-log 0
